# Batch files are executed by cmd.exe, which resumes a batch file by byte
# offset. LF-only endings, combined with the multi-byte UTF-8 these files
# carry, make cmd resume mid-token and run the tail of a command - "t" out of
# "set", "ul" out of "nul". Keep the bytes exactly as committed.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text

# The macOS launcher is a shell script: LF endings, always.
*.command text eol=lf
